# Shell scripts MUST keep LF endings, whatever core.autocrlf says.
#
# This is not a tidiness preference. With CRLF, `set -euo pipefail` becomes
# `set -euo pipefail\r` and bash rejects it as "invalid option name", so the
# script dies on line 1. It bit on the Seta core after a `git reset --hard`,
# which rewrote the working tree through autocrlf: scripts/run_sim.sh still ran
# under the MSYS bash on PATH but failed under the Git bash a Python subprocess
# picked, so the same script passed interactively and failed from a wrapper.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for anything else with a shebang or a strict parser -- but
# SCOPED to this project's own scripts. A bare `*.tcl` also matches sys/*.tcl,
# which is vendored MiSTer framework code; rewriting its line endings would
# diverge from upstream Template_MiSTer for no benefit and make the next sys/
# update a needless conflict.
scripts/**/*.tcl text eol=lf
scripts/**/*.lua text eol=lf

# Verilog/VHDL and docs are read by tools that do not care; leave them to
# core.autocrlf so Windows editors behave normally.

# VENDORED SOURCE IS STORED BYTE-FOR-BYTE.
#
# `-text` turns off all end-of-line conversion, in both directions. Without it
# `core.autocrlf` normalises on commit and converts back on checkout, so a
# vendored file is no longer byte-identical to the upstream commit its
# PROVENANCE.md names -- and two of TG68K.C's four files have MIXED CRLF and LF
# endings upstream, which a round trip silently makes uniform. That would turn
# "verbatim at <commit>" from a checkable claim into a hopeful one, and the
# whole point of vendoring verbatim first is that `git log -p` on the directory
# is then an exact record of every local divergence.
#
# Add a line here for each vendored directory as it lands.
rtl/cpu/tg68k/** -text
rtl/video/k054338/** -text
rtl/video/k053252/** -text
rtl/jtframe/** -text
sim/jtframe_ver/** -text
sim/k053252_tb/053252.v -text
sim/k053252_tb/74163.v -text
sim/k053252_tb/test.v -text
rtl/video/k055673/** -text
rtl/video/k056832/** -text
tools/jtframe/src/** -text
rtl/hiscore/*.v* -text

# Patches for other repositories apply byte-for-byte (git am / patch).
docs/patches/*.patch -text
